From 259d21efb8d29abd1d4e531f6d17c6d06f04771d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jose Bail <jose.ars.bail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:59:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ALIGN: bidirectional offset sweep cancels the friction
 load angle

The forward-only open-loop sweep baked the rotor's friction load angle into
the captured sensor offset (rotor trails the carrier by delta, so the sensor
then reads AHEAD of the true rotor by delta). On the Teknic bench this was
the whole ~-11 deg "observer bias": a +/-1000 rad/s direction test showed
it was direction-independent (-11.2 +/- 0.5 deg on both observers), i.e. in
the reference, not in the observers or the DRV8305.

ALIGN_RAMP_BIDIR (default 1): sweep ALIGN_RAMP_MECH_REVS forward, hold
ALIGN_REVERSE_DWELL_S (0.3 s) so both passes start from rest, sweep the same
backward; average the two direction means with equal weight. New RO param
align_delta (0x0137) = half the pass difference = the measured load angle.

Bench 2026-10-09: align_delta = 11.52 deg. Shadow theta_err after the fix:
flux +4.00 / +0.35 / -0.11 deg and SMO -0.69 / -0.91 / -0.80 deg at
500 / 1000 / 1500 rad/s elec (was -7..-12 deg); +/-1000 rad/s within 0.75 deg.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
